Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2010=20patch=200040=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20force-DSP-pause=20for=20fps=20upper-bound=20measure?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ment?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1 env var. Strict-1 match
per CLAUDE.md convention. When set, SoundBlaster OpenDevice issues a
DSP pause command at init (immediately after auto-init DMA starts +
IRQ hook installs) and PlayDevice's auto-resume on subsequent ring
writes is gated off. Result: DSP stays paused for the entire run;
IRQ-5 stops firing; gameplay is silent (no music synthesis, no
Pixtone SFX through the DAC).

Purpose: fps-upper-bound data point for the W22-WB-A-r2 PLAY4 iter.
Measures the absolute fps headroom the future Stage 3 (WB) + Stage 4
(OPL3) hardware-offload backends can approach when music is genuinely
off-DMA — by removing the ~13.5 ms / flip IRQ-5 wall-clock cost (per
W20A2 ablation, memory audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md) without
waiting for those backends' Stage 2/3 implementation work to land.

Trade-off: gameplay is silent. Dev-only; not user-facing.

Implementation reuses existing patch 0037+0038 idle-pause primitives:
  - g_dos_audio_pause_request flag set + MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests
    called at OpenDevice → issues DSP 0xD5 (16-bit) or 0xD0 (8-bit)
    per soundblaster_is_sb16, sets isr_dsp_paused = true.
  - PlayDevice auto-resume gated on !g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause →
    when force-pause active, ring writes don't trigger DSP 0xD6/0xD4.
  - Idle-pause auto-engagement irrelevant (DSP already paused; the
    silent-IRQ counter never reaches threshold because IRQs aren't
    firing once paused).

Init banner logged at SDL_Log INFO so DEBUG.LOG / SDLDBG.LOG document
the active mode per run:
  "audio: DSP forcefully paused via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1;
   gameplay will be silent; expect IRQ-5 to stop firing for fps comparison"

g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause flag locked in OpenDevice's lock-block
alongside other Phase 10 state vars.

Future Stage 2/3 (WB / OPL3) backends ignore this hint cleanly: their
music is hardware-routed; the SB16 ring stays empty regardless of
this flag; idle-pause auto-engages anyway. Force-pause is just a
more aggressive form of idle-pause that doesn't wait for the
silent-IRQ-threshold (4 IRQs ~92 ms).

BOOT.md entry added per env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md (dev-only
category; documents trade-off + intended use; references patch
0040 + PHASE10-DESIGN.md § E.2).

Defaults OFF preserves Phase 9 / current-build behavior bit-identical.

Modifies vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c only; no new files.
docs/BOOT.md edit lives in the parent doskutsu repo (not in this
vendor commit).

CloseDevice quit-hang fix (post-W22-WB-A-r2 operator report):
PLAY4 with force-DSP-pause active hangs on quit. Root cause: standard
CloseDevice teardown issues 0xDA (exit auto-init DMA) + 0xD3 (turn
off speaker) while the DSP is in 0xD5-paused state from OpenDevice's
force-pause. The 0xDA "exit auto-init DMA" command waits for in-flight
DMA to complete; with DMA paused, that never happens → spin → lockup.
Negative control: PLAYs 1/2/3 (Organya, no force-pause) all quit
cleanly to DOS, confirming the issue is force-pause-path-only.

Fix: at CloseDevice entry, if g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause is set,
clear it + request resume + service via MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests.
After this block, DSP is back in normal "running auto-init DMA" state
and the standard 0xDA / 0xD3 sequence completes cleanly. Idempotent
when force-pause was never engaged (isr_dsp_paused is false; service
is a no-op). ~10 LOC + comment block; no new env vars; no new state.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 77 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 75 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index dabeddb34..3856acc43 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -172,6 +172,21 @@ static volatile uint32_t isr_consecutive_silent_irqs = 0;
 static volatile bool isr_dsp_paused = false; /* set/cleared by non-IRQ service path */
 static Uint64 s_dsp_pause_start_ns = 0;      /* set when pause issued; read at resume to compute paused_ns */
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0040): force-DSP-pause for fps-upper-
+   bound measurement. When SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1,
+   the audio backend issues DSP pause at init and PlayDevice's auto-
+   resume is disabled — the DSP stays paused regardless of ring fills.
+   Gameplay becomes silent; IRQ-5 stops firing; the resulting fps is
+   the upper bound that future Stage 2/3 backends (WB / OPL3) can
+   approach when music is genuinely offloaded.
+
+   Trade-off: gameplay is silent. This is dev-only; not user-facing.
+   Defaults OFF; env var unset = current behavior bit-identical.
+
+   Per env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md: documented in docs/BOOT.md
+   as dev-only category. Strict-1 env-var match per CLAUDE.md. */
+static volatile bool g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause = false;
+
 // ISR-visible ring buffer state (all memory-locked).
 static volatile int isr_ring_read = 0;
 static volatile int isr_ring_write = 0;
@@ -589,6 +604,10 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
        context only reads. */
     DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_audio_timer_mode);
     DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_audio_timer_tsc_mhz);
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0040): force-DSP-pause flag.
+       Read by PlayDevice (non-IRQ context) but defensively locked
+       in case any future path reads it from IRQ context. */
+    DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause);
 
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0039): initialize the IRQ-safe
        timer for audio_irq_wall_us measurement. Detects RDTSC (Pentium+)
@@ -659,6 +678,32 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     }
 
     SDL_Log("SoundBlaster opened!");
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0040): force-DSP-pause for fps-
+       upper-bound measurement. When SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1,
+       request DSP pause immediately + suppress PlayDevice auto-resume.
+       Resulting fps is the absolute upper bound the future Stage 2/3
+       hardware-offload backends can approach.
+
+       Strict-1 env-var match per CLAUDE.md "Strict env-var matching
+       convention". Default OFF preserves current behavior bit-identical. */
+    {
+        const char *e = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE");
+        if (e && e[0] == '1' && e[1] == 0) {
+            g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause = true;
+            SDL_Log("audio: DSP forcefully paused via "
+                    "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1; gameplay "
+                    "will be silent; expect IRQ-5 to stop firing for fps "
+                    "comparison");
+            /* Issue DSP pause via the existing service path. The pause
+               request flag triggers WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xD5/0xD0) +
+               sets isr_dsp_paused = true. PlayDevice's auto-resume is
+               gated on !g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause so the DSP stays
+               paused regardless of subsequent ring writes. */
+            g_dos_audio_pause_request = true;
+            MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests();
+        }
+    }
     return true;
 }
 
@@ -698,8 +743,13 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
        means the audio writer has fresh data to play — almost certainly
        a Pixtone SFX trigger. Request resume; service it now so the new
        data starts playing immediately rather than after the next
-       WaitDevice cycle. */
-    if (isr_dsp_paused) {
+       WaitDevice cycle.
+
+       DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0040): suppress auto-resume when
+       force-DSP-pause is active. Force-pause is the fps-upper-bound
+       measurement mode; gameplay is silent; ring writes from any
+       source (including Pixtone) are dropped on the floor. */
+    if (isr_dsp_paused && !g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause) {
         g_dos_audio_resume_request = true;
         MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests();
     }
@@ -711,6 +761,29 @@ static void DOSSOUNDBLASTER_CloseDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
 {
     struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
     if (hidden) {
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0040): release force-DSP-pause
+           before the standard teardown sequence runs. Background:
+           OpenDevice issues DSP 0xD5 (16-bit) or 0xD0 (8-bit) when
+           SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1, leaving the DSP
+           in paused state for the entire run. The standard teardown
+           below issues 0xDA (exit auto-init DMA) which expects the
+           DMA to be active — when the DSP is paused, 0xDA spins
+           waiting for an in-flight DMA that never completes, hanging
+           the quit path. Operator W22-WB-A-r2 PLAY4 confirmed: ESC →
+           Quit → system lockup, only force-pause path affected.
+
+           Fix: clear the force-pause flag + request resume + service
+           it from non-IRQ context. After this block, the DSP is back
+           in the normal "running auto-init DMA" state and the standard
+           0xDA / 0xD3 sequence completes cleanly. Idempotent — when
+           force-pause was never engaged, isr_dsp_paused is false and
+           MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests is a no-op. */
+        if (g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause) {
+            g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause = false;
+            g_dos_audio_resume_request = true;
+            MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests();
+        }
+
         // Disable PCM.
         if (hidden->is_16bit) {
             WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0xDA); // exit 16-bit auto-init DMA
-- 
